  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "This crop name travelled between languages. The longer Akkadian and Ugaritic forms and the shorter West Semitic forms leave the direction of the earliest borrowing uncertain. Blažek discusses later transmission into Arabic and Ethiopic in item 19. The index also counts personal names, places and the Syrian god Rimmon at 2Ki.5.18 under the fruit’s spelling."
